# Portal playground - bonus
# Run: ./miniRT_bonus bonus/scenes/portal_playground.rt
#
# A wide, open-topped room you can riddle with portals. Every wall and the floor
# is a plane, so each one is BOTH a collision surface and a valid portal target.
#
# Controls:
#   left click a wall/floor  -> drop a portal (two max; 3rd recycles the oldest)
#   left click a cube        -> pick it up; it follows the cursor, click to drop
#   middle click while held  -> throw it (velocity + spin)
#   left click a sphere      -> shove it forward
#   SPACE                    -> launch whatever is under the screen centre
#
# Fun test: portal on the floor under the ledge + portal on the far wall, then
# knock a cube off the ledge and watch it shoot out across the room.
#
# Number formats per element are described above each line below.

# C  position(x,y,z)  view_direction(x,y,z)  field_of_view(degrees)
C  0,8,-26    0,-0.12,1   60

# A  ambient_ratio(0..1)  sky_colour(r,g,b 0..255) -> fills shadows / escaped rays
A  0.25       160,175,205

# qu  Q=corner(x,y,z)  u=first_edge_vector  v=second_edge_vector  colour(r,g,b)  [material]
# Here the material keyword "light" turns this quad into an area light; the quad
# spans the parallelogram Q, Q+u, Q+v, Q+u+v. Big + high = soft, even lighting.
qu -24,72,-28 30,0,0      0,0,30        180,176,168  light

# pl  point_on_plane(x,y,z)  normal(x,y,z)  colour(r,g,b)  [material]
# Planes are infinite. No material keyword -> static, so each is a collider too.
# floor
pl 0,0,0      0,1,0       195,195,200
# back wall (normal points toward the camera, -z)
pl 0,0,24     0,0,-1      175,180,205
# left wall (red), normal points right (+x)
pl -28,0,0    1,0,0       205,70,70
# right wall (blue), normal points left (-x)
pl 28,0,0     -1,0,0      70,160,205
# front wall behind the camera, normal points forward (+z)
pl 0,0,-32    0,0,1       175,180,205

# bx  centre(x,y,z)  size(width_x,height_y,depth_z)  colour(r,g,b)  [material]
# "wood" = static/immovable scenery (great flat faces to slap portals on).
# static ledge to drop props off (6x6x6, sits on the floor)
# bx -9,3,11    6,6,6       150,120,80    wood
# tall standing pillar (5 wide, 18 tall, 5 deep) - a vertical face for portals
bx 12,9,2     5,18,5      165,168,175   wood

# bx (dynamic): "brick"/"rubber" are dynamic rigid bodies (fall, tumble, collide)
# brick cube resting on the ledge (3x3x3)
bx -9,7.5,11  3,3,3       225,120,55    brick
# bouncy rubber cube on the floor (3x3x3)
bx 5,2,5      3,3,3       120,205,120   rubber
# small brick cube on the floor (2.5x2.5x2.5)
bx 9,2.5,9    2.5,2.5,2.5 210,205,90    brick

# sp  centre(x,y,z)  diameter  colour(r,g,b)  [material]
# heavy metal sphere - left-click to shove it
# sp 0,3,3      3           220,220,235   metal
